ggml-cpu, repack.cpp: raise the x16 mixed-expert bound from 256 to 512 experts.

REQUIRED to run GLM-5.3-Flash with the published engine. Reported 2026-09-21 by an outside tester on a dual-socket
Cascade Lake machine, who hit it on the first launch with the profiles in this repository.

The two dynamic work-item loops in the x16 repack path size their active-expert list on the stack and assert the bound:

    int active[256]; int n_active = 0;
    GGML_ASSERT(n_as <= 256);

GLM-5.3-Flash has 288 routed experts (its `ffn_moe_gate` weight is [4096, 512, 288]), so every mixed-expert matmul aborts
as soon as the first token is decoded:

    ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp:7450: GGML_ASSERT(n_as <= 256) failed
    ... tensor_traits_x16::forward_mul_mat_id ...

The abort comes from a worker thread inside the graph, after the model has loaded and printed its tensor table, so it reads
like a model or quantisation problem rather than a fixed array bound.

Raising both bounds to 512 is what the measured runtime on the four-socket host has always used: its private repack object
carries `int active[512]` at both sites, which is why the recorded results were never affected and the published engine was
never exercised at this expert count. The arrays are 2 KiB of stack per worker at 512.

Applies to the `llama.cpp-glm5n-goal-0904` bundle (base `2e0e57f1` of unslothai/llama.cpp plus
`engineering/2026-09-12/patches/llama.cpp-glm5n-goal-0904.patch`). Verified: both sites are unique in that source, the file
passes `g++ -fsyntax-only`, and the same values run 288 experts in production.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp
index da7dd87..52f525f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp
@@ -7446,8 +7446,8 @@ class tensor_traits_x16 : public tensor_traits_base {
         ggml_barrier(params->threadpool);
         constexpr int64_t tile = 64;
         const int64_t n_tiles = (nr0 + tile - 1) / tile;
-        int active[256]; int n_active = 0;
-        GGML_ASSERT(n_as <= 256);
+        int active[512]; int n_active = 0;
+        GGML_ASSERT(n_as <= 512);
         for (int e = 0; e < n_as; ++e) {
             if (counts[e] > 0) active[n_active++] = e;
         }
@@ -7521,8 +7521,8 @@ class tensor_traits_x16 : public tensor_traits_base {
         // shared with another process does not stall the whole socket at the next barrier.
         constexpr int64_t tile = 64;
         const int64_t n_tiles = (n_out + tile - 1) / tile;
-        int active[256]; int n_active = 0;
-        GGML_ASSERT(n_experts <= 256);
+        int active[512]; int n_active = 0;
+        GGML_ASSERT(n_experts <= 512);
         for (int64_t e = 0; e < n_experts; ++e) {
             if (counts[e] > 0) active[n_active++] = (int) e;
         }
